  \caption{\textbf{Strong pooled ESM-2 baselines in the 1024-residue Gold experiment.}
  Absolute AUROC for the six matched training/test-negative constructions.
  The sum-plus-absolute-difference logistic control uses pair-dependent features;
  the sum-only control is strictly additive. PPI models show mean AUROC over
  seeds 11, 22, 33, while each logistic control is a single fitted classifier
  per training construction (not three independent seed fits). The degree-matched
  Gold test is degenerate for train-network degree and is shown only as a diagnostic.
  Different negative constructions do not form independent replicates.}
  \label{fig:baseline-comparison}
\end{figure*}

\section{Limitations}
The 512- and 1024-residue experiments retain only 16.3\
Gold training positives. We test four implementations and one pLM family;
pretraining may expose held-out proteins. Negative labels do not establish
non-interaction (Appendix~\ref{sec:limitations-detail}).

